      "why": "pipelined_m is my only family that has produced a design on the merged front (959 luts+ffs), beating the full pipelined (1273). The key to area is minimizing the number of register stages (m) while keeping Fmax high enough for >=1 MSPS. I focus m in 2..8 (larger m = fewer registers = less area, but tighter timing), n_iter in 10..18 (enough for 2^-10 error with modest guards), and data_width 12..18 (12 is the minimum that can hit 2^-10 with enough n_iter; going higher wastes area). Guards are kept low (frac 0..2, angle -1..1) to save bits, since accuracy is dominated by n_iter and data_width."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.5,
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {
